<PageLayout title='BIOATLAS' kicker='PROJECT // IN DEVELOPMENT' lead='A navigable atlas for biodiversity, evolution and natural history.'>
<section><div class="prose content-page"><p>BIOATLAS is conceived as an interactive scientific platform rather than a static species encyclopedia. The visitor should be able to move across maps, phylogenies, time, traits and stories to understand where an organism fits in the history of life.</p><h2>$ mission</h2><p>Build an accessible digital environment where biodiversity data become spatial, evolutionary and narrative experiences.</p><h2>$ planned_modules</h2><ul><li>Interactive species and locality maps</li><li>Phylogenetic navigation that avoids presenting evolution as a ladder toward humans</li><li>Deep-time and fossil context</li><li>Species profiles connected to ecology, traits and evolutionary questions</li><li>3D fossil or specimen experiences where suitable</li><li>Open educational layers for classrooms and public exploration</li></ul><h2>$ working_stack</h2><p>Python, GeoPandas, QGIS, Rasterio, Shapely and web mapping/visualization technologies, with public geographic data where licensing permits.</p></div></section>
</PageLayout>